  "armor_paint": "Native body crops light the fitted solid plates; native palette materials separate ridges, fingers and articulated seams. Brown shaft pixels (R>1.4G and R>1.4B) are separated from the armor derivative before nearest native-color extension of transparent pixels. Retained opaque plate paint and archive masters stay intact. Unseen backs reuse the recovered view.",
  "mirror_glass": "Native static reflection crop excludes the original attached flowers; the solid mirror keeps the painted reflection planar.",
  "flowers": "Original sprite petal/leaf palettes and pot paint; 3D clusters reuse immutable Wind Meadow flower GLBs with owned vertex-color copies. Branch depth and unseen shapes are fitted.",
  "method": "Native curtain cloth/canopy paint follows shared folded geometry; traced native cords wrap those same folds. Native friezes and small pedestal faces also supply separate bounded relief. Native column faces and framed picture art rectified without black tops; shared box/face geometry retains source placements. Native bookcase fronts rectified without black isometric tops; existing modular boxes and ledges supply depth. Blue pedestal ornaments retain original cropped pixels."
}
